  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Let $a\\geq0$ and $m,n\\in\\mathbb{N}$. Prove that $(a^{1/n})^{1/m}=a^{1/(nm)}$. Hint: evaluate $((a^{1/n})^{1/m})^{mn}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(a^{1/n})^{1/m}=a^{1/(nm)}$.\n\nThe nonnegative nested root has $mn$th power $a$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\bigl((a^{1/n})^{1/m}\\bigr)^{mn}&=\\bigl(\\sqrt[m]{\\sqrt[n]{a}}\\bigr)^{mn}\\\\\\bigl((a^{1/n})^{1/m}\\bigr)^{mn}&=\\bigl((\\sqrt[m]{\\sqrt[n]{a}})^m\\bigr)^n\\\\\\bigl((a^{1/n})^{1/m}\\bigr)^{mn}&=(\\sqrt[n]{a})^n\\\\\\bigl((a^{1/n})^{1/m}\\bigr)^{mn}&=a\\end{align*}$$\nThe nested root is nonnegative. Taking the nonnegative $mn$th root gives\n$$\\begin{align*}(a^{1/n})^{1/m}&=\\sqrt[mn]{a}\\\\(a^{1/n})^{1/m}&=a^{1/(nm)}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 63
  },
